invariant: INV-17
file: src/record.c
catches: aes_suite_test
reason: rec_dir_init_suite does not wipe the direction's stored powers before
  it keys, so a direction keyed under ChaCha20, or under a ch_cfg.cpu
  without CH_CPU_CONSTANT_TIME_AES, after an AES-GCM key keeps the powers
  of that key's hash subkey, which is as secret as the key. No record reads
  them there, so every record is right. bin/aes_suite_test keys one
  direction that way and requires 256 zero bytes
  (test/ghash_powers_tests.h, docs/decisions.md 234).

--- old
    ct_wipe(d->schedule, sizeof d->schedule);
    ct_wipe(d->ghash_powers, sizeof d->ghash_powers);
--- new
    ct_wipe(d->schedule, sizeof d->schedule);
